.TH "FWD PORTS" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd ports Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-ports \- Open, list, or close loopback-only local ports forwarded
to a running session.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd ports
[OPTIONS] [arguments]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open, list, or close loopback-only local ports forwarded to a running session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-name <str>
Exact session name; defaults to shared positional selectors or the
current project.
.TP
\fB\-\-ls\fP
Alias for fwd ls --ports; one optional selector narrows it to a session.
.TP
\fB\-\-close\fP
Close listed local ports, or every forward for the selected/current
session when no ports are listed.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-projects\fP
List or close forwarding across every locally tracked project.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP <auto|rich|markdown|json>
In listing mode, choose the output format.  [default: auto]
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fP
Render structured output as JSON; shorthand for --format json.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
